    "case_id": "705",
    "case_summary": "A 28-year-old pregnant woman (G2P0) at 16 weeks and 4 days of gestation presented with fever for four days. She had initially visited a local community hospital where she was diagnosed with an upper respiratory tract infection. The fever persisted along with general weakness and appetite loss, prompting her to seek care at our hospital.\n\nVital signs were normal except for an axillary temperature >38.7°C. Other physical examination findings, including cervical and fetal examination, were normal.\n\n{'Laboratory Tests': ['- WBC: 8.06 × 109 cells/L (Neu 78.1%, Ly 14.0%, and Mo 7.7%)', '- CRP: 11.5 mg/L', '- PCT: 0.22 ng/mL', '- Urine and liver function tests: normal', '- Blood culture: positive (identified using MALDI-TOF mass spectrometry)', '- Vaginal swabs: negative for pathogens'], 'Molecular Testing': ['- Serotyping identified serovars 1/2b, 3b, and 7', '- MLST analysis performed on seven housekeeping genes', '- Virulence gene amplification of ten genes completed']}",
